00:54:35,000 --> 00:54:41,000
But the company gets either at or below
sector average earnings growth.

342
00:54:41,000 --> 00:54:50,000
So negative earnings growth in period two,
like in period one, but in the second
period, it's either at or below the sector
average.

343
00:54:50,000 --> 00:54:54,000
This just isn't worth looking at at all.

344
00:54:54,000 --> 00:55:12,000
Now, from a classic kind of portfolio
management perspective, this is the type
of earnings growth profile that could
provide investors with a hedge to a high
quality long idea in the same sector.

345
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:17,000
However, we are not investors and we are
not in the hedging game.

346
00:55:17,000 --> 00:55:24,000
We want to be, as traders, long, great
stocks that go up a lot.

347
00:55:24,000 --> 00:55:30,000
And we want to be short, terrible, crappy
stocks that go down a lot.

348
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:34,000
We always should be looking to optimize.

349
00:55:34,000 --> 00:55:43,000
So we do not go into positions, into long
positions, and then put short hedges
against them.

350
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:54,000
We don't need them because, as traders, we
should be always looking for shorts that
are actually going down, looking for bad
stocks.

351
00:55:54,000 --> 00:55:57,000
So we'll learn about this in the next
video.

352
00:55:58,000 --> 00:56:05,000
We want to be keeping volatility high in
the portfolio and correlation as low as
possible.

353
00:56:05,000 --> 00:56:08,000
And we want to be avoiding hedges wherever
possible.

354
00:56:08,000 --> 00:56:18,000
We would much rather be short cross sector
than intrasector and shorting stuff just
for the sake of shorting it to have a
hedge.

355
00:56:19,000 --> 00:56:28,000
And shorting something in the same sector
just because it's in the same sector and
it looks bad on paper isn't the way we
want to go.

356
00:56:28,000 --> 00:56:41,000
We would much rather be cross sector and
shorting genuinely bad stocks that are
going to go down rather than looking for a
generic hedge in the same sector.

357
00:56:41,000 --> 00:56:47,000
And when looking for shorts, we should be
looking at much higher market cap.

358
00:56:47,000 --> 00:56:54,000
And as mentioned, more of this will come
later in the next video.

359
00:56:54,000 --> 00:57:04,000
Now let's have a look at cases 7, 8, 9 and
10 visually so we fully understand them.

