367
00:57:49,000 --> 00:57:51,000
We are not optimizing.

368
00:57:52,000 --> 00:58:03,000
Our next case is case number 8, which is
our first turnaround story, where again,
this company has positive EPS.

369
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:09,000
But in the first period, they have
negative earnings growth.

370
00:58:09,000 --> 00:58:12,000
That's below the sector average.

371
00:58:12,000 --> 00:58:16,000
Then in the second period, they have
positive earnings growth.

372
00:58:16,000 --> 00:58:19,000
That's around the sector average.

373
00:58:19,000 --> 00:58:31,000
So what's happening to this company is
that they're having a year where their
earnings growth is negative.

374
00:58:31,000 --> 00:58:34,000
And then they're turning it around and
it's going positive.

375
00:58:34,000 --> 00:58:42,000
And it's forecasted to be somewhere around
the sector average in the second period,
year two.

376
00:58:42,000 --> 00:58:46,000
We would define this as a turnaround
story.

377
00:58:46,000 --> 00:58:57,000
Now, our next case, case number nine, is
our turnaround story on steroids.

378
00:58:57,000 --> 00:59:01,000
So it's our turbo turnaround story.

379
00:59:01,000 --> 00:59:07,000
This is the earnings growth profile where
the company is actually loss making.

380
00:59:07,000 --> 00:59:17,000
They have negative EPS and they have
negative earnings growth that's below
sector average in the first period.

381
00:59:17,000 --> 00:59:27,000
And then in the second period, they have a
massive turnaround in EPS that goes from
negative EPS to positive EPS.

382
00:59:27,000 --> 00:59:36,000
And they have extremely high positive
earnings growth that's way above the
sector average.

383
00:59:36,000 --> 00:59:49,000
So these turnaround stories, case number
eight and case number nine, because of the
magnitude of these moves in earnings
growth, they do get our attention.

384
00:59:49,000 --> 01:00:15,000
And they could be quite interesting to us
