398
01:01:56,000 --> 01:02:00,000
But let's close the loop here on long
trade ideas.

399
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:22,000
We always want to be optimizing and we
want to be making sure that we have
valuation and earnings growth that is
evident that the market likes the stock
that we're looking at when we're
attempting to identify positive outliers
in the sector.

400
01:02:22,000 --> 01:02:46,000
So if you think back to the tables that we
looked at in previous videos where we
mapped out an entire sector and we had all
of our metrics that we look at in the
spreadsheet where we had price earnings
ratio, earnings growth and we had peg
ratio and market capitalization.

401
01:02:46,000 --> 01:02:55,000
Now, for long ideas, we will have a market
capitalization filter.

402
01:02:55,000 --> 01:02:58,000
We will always lean towards mid caps.

403
01:02:58,000 --> 01:03:03,000
We are looking in that $3 to $10 billion
market cap space.

404
01:03:03,000 --> 01:03:13,000
What we will also filter for is what we
filter for for long ideas in our first
step, like we did in previous videos.

405
01:03:13,000 --> 01:03:23,000
First, we will filter for PE and we will
then filter for earnings growth both in
period one and in period two.

406
01:03:23,000 --> 01:03:26,000
And what are we looking for in the ideal
situation?

407
01:03:26,000 --> 01:03:39,000
We are looking for PE on a premium to the
sector in period one and then PE on a
premium to the sector in period two.

408
01:03:39,000 --> 01:03:48,000
But the PE is lower in period two than in
period one, both for the stock and both
for the sector.

409
01:03:48,000 --> 01:03:57,000
For both the stock and the sector, this is
evidence that EPS is going higher.

410
01:03:57,000 --> 01:04:07,000
And for the stock itself, it is evidence
that the market likes the stock and
prefers the stock and pays a premium to
the sector.

411
01:04:07,000 --> 01:04:16,000
Additionally, we will filter for earnings
growth percentage.

412
01:04:16,000 --> 01:04:26,000
And what we want to see in the ideal
scenario is for the stock to have positive
earnings growth that is higher than the
sector in period one.

413
01:04:26,000 --> 01:04:39,000
And then in period two, the stock earnings
growth in period two is higher than its
earnings growth in period one and higher
than the sector.

414
01:04:39,000 --> 01:04:49,000
Additionally, we want to see that earnings
growth in the sector overall is actually
trending higher as well.

415
01:04:49,000 --> 01:05:00,000
So, for our case one, our ideal earnings
growth profile for long-idea quantitative
processing.

416
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:14,000
When we are looking to identify positive
outliers, our ideal case, case number one,
is for sequentially positive, above-sector
average earnings growth momentum.

417
01:05:14,000 --> 01:05:26,000
And when we are also working through our
long-idea processing, we also consider and
identify our case number two and our case
number three.

418
01:05:26,000 --> 01:05:43,000
Now, all of these cases, as you know, we
have identified as optimal situations for
long-idea processing with the ideal being
sequentially positive, above-sector
average earnings growth momentum.

419
01:05:43,000 --> 01:05:52,000
But remember, in these three cases, the
EPS is positive.

420
01:05:52,000 --> 01:05:55,000
We are not coming from a loss-making
situation.

421
01:05:55,000 --> 01:05:58,000
The company is making profit.

422
01:05:58,000 --> 01:06:06,000
So, we have positive EPS and positive
earnings growth in all of those cases.

423
01:06:06,000 --> 01:06:15,000
And this is, of course, evidenced by the
backdrop of the valuation in period two
versus period one.

424
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:21,000
So, a lower PE in period two versus period
one.

425
01:06:21,000 --> 01:06:26,000
The EPS is going to be higher in period
two.

426
01:06:26,000 --> 01:06:44,000
Therefore, when we take the stock price
today and we divide it by EPS one, the PE
is going to be higher in period one versus
when we take the same stock price of the
current day and divide it by EPS two.

427
01:06:44,000 --> 01:06:53,000
Because EPS two is higher, we're going to
get a lower PE ratio versus PE one.

428
01:06:53,000 --> 01:07:05,000
So, we should always be thinking in terms
of forward-looking fundamentals, earnings
growth momentum, and in terms of price
momentum.

429
01:07:05,000 --> 01:07:16,000
So, we try to concentrate on price and the
fundamentals and valuation that is behind
price and that is driving price.

430
01:07:16,000 --> 01:07:28,000
So, the difference between PE two and PE
one is the gap that the stock needs to go
up to maintain the same PE ratio.

431
01:07:28,000 --> 01:07:43,000
So, it's the price movement from period
one to period two in order to maintain the
same PE in period two as in period one
with the new forecasted EPS.

432
01:07:43,000 --> 01:07:57,000
So, what is happening is the company, when
they're moving from period one to period
two, they are hitting their EPS and
earnings growth percentage guidance.

433
01:07:57,000 --> 01:08:02,000
And by the way, this type of analysis also
applies to PEG ratios.

434
01:08:02,000 --> 01:08:19,000
The difference between PEG two and PEG one
is the amount that the PE ratio has to go
up from period one to period two in order
to maintain the same PEG ratio.

435
01:08:19,000 --> 01:08:26,000
So, this is how we always have to be
thinking about it as traders.

436
01:08:26,000 --> 01:08:40,000
We always want to be thinking in terms of
price momentum and the fundamentals that
are driving the price momentum and the
potential upside over the period.

437
01:08:40,000 --> 01:09:02,000
So, when we are processing for our long
ideas in our quant processing phase and we
are identifying potential long trade
ideas, we want to see really good, strong,
sequentially positive above sector average
earnings growth momentum.

438
01:09:02,000 --> 01:09:14,000
And we also want to see evidence from the
valuation from the PE that the market is
aware of this too and they are paying a
premium for the stock.

439
01:09:14,000 --> 01:09:28,000
Which means if the stock delivers in
period two or in the process of going from
period one to period two, it looks like
increasingly that the stock is going to
deliver on its earnings.

440
01:09:28,000 --> 01:09:39,000
The price is going to close the gap and
the market is going to pay the same or
higher valuation in period two versus
period one.

